{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought","id":1490327,"title":"I bought...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-15T18:27:46-07:00","id":1490327,"title":"I bought...","content":"...the Trinity Continuum Core Rulebook and the Trinity Continuum Aeon Core Rulebook. <br /> <br /> I played this line of games way back when they first came out, but never got into the d20 versions. But, now that\u2019s changed! Yay! It feels like coming home.<br /> <br /> Is Aether part of the main timeline? The TC Core mentions alternate timelines, so I was wondering if Aether is like Marvel\u2019s \u201cWhat If...\u201d stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T18:47:19-07:00","id":1490332,"title":"","content":"Aether is part of the time line, it happens in 1895.<br /> <br /> The thing with the Continuum is the past is defined, so Aether is the past of Adventure, but Adventure don\u2019t need to be the future of Aether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T18:48:34-07:00","id":1490333,"title":"","content":"How do they cover up a Martian invasion, though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T18:59:02-07:00","id":1490334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490333#post1490333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do they cover up a Martian invasion, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll presumably find out tomorrow when the setting secrets chapter is released.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T21:42:49-07:00","id":1490351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490333#post1490333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do they cover up a Martian invasion, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Temporal continuity in the Aether setting is less than stable","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T05:15:48-07:00","id":1490372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490333#post1490333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do they cover up a Martian invasion, though?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not to spoil anything about the game, let's just say that the unique properties of Aether allow one to undo the changes it brought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9255-docsteve2020","name":"DocSteve2020","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T07:34:08-07:00","id":1490393,"title":"","content":"There's a section in one of the chapters about Unwinding Time, where \u00c6ther-related events can retroactively be removed from the timeline \u2014 partially, at least. It's not just an alteration of memories; people who were killed by the Unwound Event are usually alive once it has been Unwound. But it's also not a \u201cfix everything\u201d button, as the people involved in the Unwound incident still remember that <i>something</i> happened; just not precisely <i>what</i>. <br /> <br /> So they can Unwind the destruction of Paris, and the residents who were killed by it are back; but they're aware that something bad happened, even if they can't put their finger on just what that something is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T08:23:49-07:00","id":1490399,"title":"","content":"Ok! Cool! I like everything this thread has mentioned! So...is Aether a form of Flux? Is there an event that triggers the spread of Aether?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-16-2022, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T09:07:07-07:00","id":1490402,"title":"","content":"A few more setting questions...<br /> <br /> Are psiad rules yet published? If so, where?<br /> <br /> Can psiads reach proxy-level power, or is that a benefit of being a psion?<br /> <br /> What was SK Bhurano doing in the Nova Age? Or has that yet to be revealed? I think she must\u2019ve been a psiad before the Doyen tricked her into becoming a psion. Is this true? Can other psiads be formatted in a Prometheus Tank?<br /> <br /> EDIT: After doing a bit of research, I\u2019ve more questions...<br /> <br /> Is TC Anima basically a \u201cgame-within-a-game\u201d? Does it contribute to the setting, or is it meant to be more stand-alone, considering it\u2019s very nature.<br /> <br /> When is TC Assassins set? What\u2019re the core character types? How does it fit into the overall Trinity Continuum timeline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-16-2022, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T11:03:29-07:00","id":1490407,"title":"","content":"Rules for Psiads can be found in the Aeon Expansion.<br /> <br /> Psiads are more 'broad' than the focused Psions. They can use more Modes, but are not as powerful as Psions. (I think 3 dots was the max?)<br /> <br /> Bhurano goes under a different name in Abberant, mostly doing science stuff (investigating Quantum, etc.).<br /> <br /> Anima takes place between Abberant and Aeon. It's pretty stand-alone. Yes, you can play it as a game-within-a-game - LitRPG is one of the main inspirations. You don't HAVE to, though - a pure cyberpunk, no MMO game is certainly possible.<br /> <br /> Assassins takes place in the same undefined 'Present' as the Core setting - the other side of the coin, so to speak. Character types? You're an assassin - you kill people. The only real differentiation is your reason for killing people and your methods for doing so. If you've seen John Wick then you basically know what this is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","user":"NullApostle","date":". 08-16-2022, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T11:16:46-07:00","id":1490408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490407#post1490407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assassins takes place in the same undefined 'Present' as the Core setting - the other side of the coin, so to speak. Character types? You're an assassin - you kill people. The only real differentiation is your reason for killing people and your methods for doing so. If you've seen John Wick then you basically know what this is.</div> </div> </div> </div>... or <i><b>Asssasin's Creed</b> </i>game series - half of Societies of TC Assassins book are inspired from <b>AC</b> games - namely <b>Daughters of Jackobins</b> ( past French Revolution Assassins Order ), <b>Signal</b> ( modern and from marginalised groups Assassins ) - and <b>Society of Leonidas</b> ( based on Order of Ancients &amp; Templars ). On the other hand, russian <b>Krugu Vorvo</b> is basically society of Assasins from <i><b>John Wicks</b></i> frenchise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T11:18:11-07:00","id":1490409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490407#post1490407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rules for Psiads can be found in the Aeon Expansion.<br /> <br /> Psiads are more 'broad' than the focused Psions. They can use more Modes, but are not as powerful as Psions. (I think 3 dots was the max?)<br /> <br /> Bhurano goes under a different name in Abberant, mostly doing science stuff (investigating Quantum, etc.).<br /> <br /> Anima takes place between Abberant and Aeon. It's pretty stand-alone. Yes, you can play it as a game-within-a-game - LitRPG is one of the main inspirations. You don't HAVE to, though - a pure cyberpunk, no MMO game is certainly possible.<br /> <br /> Assassins takes place in the same undefined 'Present' as the Core setting - the other side of the coin, so to speak. Character types? You're an assassin - you kill people. The only real differentiation is your reason for killing people and your methods for doing so. If you've seen John Wick then you basically know what this is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T11:19:43-07:00","id":1490410,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve seen it mentioned a few times in relation to TC Anima...but what is \u2018Glass\u2019?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T11:29:34-07:00","id":1490412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490410#post1490410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what is \u2018Glass\u2019?</div> </div> </div> </div>GLASS Is neuralinterface inner computer implant in your brain. It's basiclly connects your brain to setting Internet 2.0 ( called OpNet ), directly brain-to-network. It can do things like those from <b>Ghost in the Shell </b>- or on this 'future tech demo' below - only you do not need any more new glasses or devices. Implant in your brain connects you to the Web... &lt;Neuromancer music \ud83d\ude0e&gt;<br /> <br /> The most popular use of GLASS in <b>Anima</b> is to play ultra popular true VR MMO called <i><b>TerraSurge</b></i> - think of it as true VR cross between <b>World of Warcraft</b> and <b>Elder Scrolls Online</b>. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> Like short film <b>Sight</b> - only you do this in your brain, no glasses needed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S. <b>Anima</b> core points that GLASS is used in 'Historical Reenactments VR Servers' - that sounds A LOT like <b>Assassin's Creed</b> as video game franchise with each next historical game - only in 'full body VR'. It's even points idea of HRS as other gamelines in Trinity Continuum chronicle. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lK_cdkpazjI\" data-code=\"lK_cdkpazjI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/lK_cdkpazjI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-16-2022, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T12:06:12-07:00","id":1490418,"title":"","content":"So, it <i>is</i> a game-within-a-game!<br /> <br /> What about TC Assassins? Is it it\u2019s own game, in the same manner at TC Aeon and TC Aberrant? Or is it merely an augmentation to TC Core?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T12:23:21-07:00","id":1490421,"title":"","content":"Assassins ARE Talents, albeit super-focused souped-up ones. It's a bit hard to classify. It technically IS its own game, insofar as the tone is VERY different to pretty much all the rest of the Continuum (much darker, as in: murder is the focus). But it's also not quite stand-alone: it takes place in the Core setting and has basically no special rules, except the Assassins' &quot;super-Gifts&quot; (called Masteries).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T12:43:15-07:00","id":1490424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490421#post1490421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assassins ARE Talents, albeit super-focused souped-up ones. It's a bit hard to classify. It technically IS its own game, insofar as the tone is VERY different to pretty much all the rest of the Continuum (much darker, as in: murder is the focus). But it's also not quite stand-alone: it takes place in the Core setting and has basically no special rules, except the Assassins' &amp;quot;super-Gifts&amp;quot; (called Masteries).</div> </div> </div> </div>It has some neat flashback rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27511-fanggrip","name":"FangGrip","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T12:46:27-07:00","id":1490425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490399#post1490399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok! Cool! I like everything this thread has mentioned! So...is Aether a form of Flux? Is there an event that triggers the spread of Aether?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aether is closely related to Flux. After reading the setting secrets, the way I would describe it is that it is Flux that has been contaminated by Quantum. It is unique to the Ascendancy, and may even be unique to that subclass of the Ascendancy known as the Martians. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">And technically, there was an event that triggered spread of \u00c6ther: the incursion of the Martians into a neighboring timeline.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T12:50:03-07:00","id":1490427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490418#post1490418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about TC Assassins? Is it it\u2019s own game, in the same manner at TC Aeon and TC Aberrant? Or is it merely an augmentation to TC Core?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>TC Assassins </b>is like big <b>John Wick/Assassins's Creed</b> stand alone DLC to your favorite S-F RPG - <b>Trinity Continuum</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> For example,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468693-tc-assasins-instead-aberrant-on-timeline\"> I'm using <b>Assassins</b> instead of normal <b>Aberrant </b>era in my own chronicle</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, <b>TC Assassins</b> lore points there should be Assassins in other TC eras, so you should also have them in<b> Aether</b>, <b>Adventure!</b>, <b>Anima </b>and <b>Aeon</b>.<br /> <br /> TC Assassins in announced<b> TC Aegis</b> looks like <b><i>Assassin's Creed: Odyssey</i> - the Table Top RPG</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-16-2022, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T12:59:39-07:00","id":1490429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FangGrip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490424#post1490424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has some neat flashback rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes. You're right. They've adapted that one from Blades in the Dark, which is one of the inspirations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T13:22:48-07:00","id":1490432,"title":"","content":"Ooo! The more I read, the more excited I get!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T13:24:25-07:00","id":1490433,"title":"","content":"Can an Aeon-Era psiad be transformed into a psion? Or was that possible because Bhurano\u2019s transformation at the Hammersmith Event?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T14:22:16-07:00","id":1490441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490433#post1490433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can an Aeon-Era psiad be transformed into a psion? Or was that possible because Bhurano\u2019s transformation at the Hammersmith Event?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes\u2026 Kind of\u2026 if the psiad wants yes, otherwise they remain as psiad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T16:08:26-07:00","id":1490451,"title":"","content":"Is Trinity Continuum like the Chronicles of Darkness, in that fan products can be sold at the Storyteller\u2019s Vault?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T17:14:24-07:00","id":1490459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490451#post1490451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Trinity Continuum like the Chronicles of Darkness, in that fan products can be sold at the Storyteller\u2019s Vault?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. There are a lot of products. It\u2019s called Storypath Nexus. Worth to take a look in them (I have 4, check my signature)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T17:45:52-07:00","id":1490462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490402#post1490402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can psiads reach proxy-level power, or is that a benefit of being a psion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Psiads can hit Psi 6 with 4 dots in the Modes of their best three Aptitudes (and can reach 5 dots in a single Mode using the right Edge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490402#post1490402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was SK Bhurano doing in the Nova Age? Or has that yet to be revealed? I think she must\u2019ve been a psiad before the Doyen tricked her into becoming a psion. Is this true?</div> </div> </div> </div>She did quantum research. IIRC the Doyen didn't trick her so much as they press ganged her. The other proxies had a choice, but she was forced into it, then immediately possessed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490402#post1490402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is TC Anima basically a \u201cgame-within-a-game\u201d? Does it contribute to the setting, or is it meant to be more stand-alone, considering it\u2019s very nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>The events of Anima lead directly to the Shanghai Accords mentioned on page 26 of the Aeon book. It is also hinted that Dr. Bhurano has a team of psiads running around in the background investigating rumors of a buried spaceship (which happens to be linked to Aether's Martian invasion). If that scenario isn't relevant to your campaign, you can skip it as an historical footnote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T10:59:15-07:00","id":1490519,"title":"","content":"Oh! Ok! Cool! I\u2019ll definitely pick up TC Anima, when it comes out.<br /> <br /> A question, though...<br /> <br /> I noticed Talents are the \u2018core\u2019 character type, and they manipulate, luck, probability and chance to do some really awesome stuff. TC Aeon mentions Talents quite a lot. Is TC Anima, TC Aberrant, TC Assassins and TC Aether the same way, making Talents the only character-type playable in every time period?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T11:07:05-07:00","id":1490521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490519#post1490519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! Ok! Cool! I\u2019ll definitely pick up TC Anima, when it comes out.<br /> <br /> A question, though...<br /> <br /> I noticed Talents are the \u2018core\u2019 character type, and they manipulate, luck, probability and chance to do some really awesome stuff. TC Aeon mentions Talents quite a lot. Is TC Anima, TC Aberrant, TC Assassins and TC Aether the same way, making Talents the only character-type playable in every time period?</div> </div> </div> </div>So far, sorta. Without some hand waving.<br /> <br /> You could play a psiad in all of them. You could play an assassin in all of them. You could play an aethernaught in all of them.<br /> <br /> It just requires a bit of narrative contrivance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27511,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27511-fanggrip","user":"FangGrip","date":". 08-17-2022, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27511-fanggrip","name":"FangGrip","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T11:30:44-07:00","id":1490524,"title":"","content":"Talents are superhuman, yet they are not really, at least they dont seam to be.<br /> <br /> They are the &quot;standard&quot; character, having basically the power of protagonism, like the heroes of action and adventure movies. When ever the theme ask for a &quot;normal person&quot; as player character, they are talking about Talents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T12:40:56-07:00","id":1490528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490519#post1490519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! Ok! Cool! I\u2019ll definitely pick up TC Anima, when it comes out.<br /> <br /> A question, though...<br /> <br /> I noticed Talents are the \u2018core\u2019 character type, and they manipulate, luck, probability and chance to do some really awesome stuff. TC Aeon mentions Talents quite a lot. Is TC Anima, TC Aberrant, TC Assassins and TC Aether the same way, making Talents the only character-type playable in every time period?</div> </div> </div> </div>I presume Talents are the default character type because:<br /> <br /> 1). An RPG's core book needs character creation rules.<br /> 2). Playing (mildly) superhuman characters is seen as cooler than playing a baseline human.<br /> 3). Daredevils were part of the original Adventure! setting.<br /> 4). The Talent mechanics are simple enough to cram into the core book without taking up much space.<br /> <br /> As a comparison, the Talent rules take up about 30 pages, Nova rules take up 50+ pages, and Psi rules take up 60+ pages. Using Talents gets you an interesting character at a lower page count, which make the core book cheaper to print.<br /> <br /> Talents also tend to be significantly weaker than most other character types, so the default assumption is that Aberrant players will probably play Novas and Aeon players will probably play Psions. Storyguides should be careful when mixing character types, as this can lead to some players almost completely dominating game sessions while others are reduced to punching out minor antagonists in the background. Even the Gift from the Aberrant book <i>The Bigger They Are</i> only lets a Talent compete with a Nova for 3-10 rounds, after which they're tapped out of Inspiration, while the Nova Antagonist will never run out of Mega-Might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T15:30:26-07:00","id":1490550,"title":"","content":"A question?<br /> <br /> In the TC Core, it mentioned Powered Edges can be taken by anybody with powers. Following this up are Enhanced Edges. While they mention the Inspired, can <i>only</i> Talents learn Enhanced Edges? Or can a psion from TC Aeon do it, too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T15:34:01-07:00","id":1490551,"title":"","content":"As far as I know any character that otherwise meets the prerequisites can buy Enhanced Edges. At the very least that is how I have run it. Otherwise Novas could never be the richest people in the world (the Loaded Edge), which seems to cut against theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T16:33:52-07:00","id":1490560,"title":"","content":"Another question, this one TC Aeon-specific.<br /> <br /> The special Edges available to those who follows a Psi Order Path? Are those available to neutrals and Talents? I think the answer is yes, but I\u2019d like to be sure,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T16:48:44-07:00","id":1490564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490560#post1490560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question, this one TC Aeon-specific.<br /> <br /> The special Edges available to those who follows a Psi Order Path? Are those available to neutrals and Talents? I think the answer is yes, but I\u2019d like to be sure,</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as it makes sense for them. The Norca Edge, for example, would only apply to a Biokinetic IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T17:31:46-07:00","id":1490566,"title":"","content":"Instead of hijacking someone else\u2019s thread, I\u2019ll limit my questions to here.<br /> <br /> Who exactly <i>do</i> you play, in TC Anima? Cyborgs? MMO players? Psiads? Or something else entirely? (Obviously, Talents\u2019ll be a playable archetype, but still.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T20:20:31-07:00","id":1490585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490566#post1490566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of hijacking someone else\u2019s thread, I\u2019ll limit my questions to here.<br /> <br /> Who exactly <i>do</i> you play, in TC Anima? Cyborgs? MMO players? Psiads? Or something else entirely? (Obviously, Talents\u2019ll be a playable archetype, but still.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The default assumption is that you're a Talent, although there are Edges to give them cybernetic implants, since this is before the Shanghai Accords, so they're not yet restricted.<br /> <br /> Dr. Bhurano and some other psiads are there looking for the Martian spaceship, but they weren't actually detailed in the manuscript, so you can make up anything you want about them if playing a psiad. Some of the psiads have to hide from the public, because they were active in the Nova Age and aberrant hunters believe them to be weak novas.<br /> <br /> There are also rumors of actual aberrants skulking about, looking for a kidnapped aberrant being experimented on by the government (a misinterpretation of traces of quantum energy leaking out of the Martian ship), so you could even play a nova campaign, although they'd need to be very discreet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T01:52:25-07:00","id":1490591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1490327-i-bought?p=1490560#post1490560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question, this one TC Aeon-specific.<br /> <br /> The special Edges available to those who follows a Psi Order Path? Are those available to neutrals and Talents? I think the answer is yes, but I\u2019d like to be sure,</div> </div> </div> </div>There are Psionic Edges that add effects to your powers and there edges that are related to the paths, some restrict to psion or even specific aptitudes, some restricted to non psions (one specific in mind is one that make you a better puppet for the Telepaths). There is a real good variety of Edges if you gather all the Aeon books (including the tasty bits).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}